==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|feithfulli}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|faithful|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfeɪθfəli/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-faithfully.wav|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[faithful]] manner.
#: ''The CD reproduces music faithfully.''
#: ''I have been faithfully married for the past twenty years.''
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1990|artist=Depeche Mode|album=Violator|title=Policy of Truth|text=You'll see your problems multiplied / if you continually decide / to '''faithfully''' pursue / the policy of truth.}}
# {{lb|en|US}} A conventional [[formula]] for ending a [[letter]], used when the [[salutation]] addresses the person for whom the letter is intended using an [[honorific]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|formula for ending correspondence}} {{l|en|yours faithfully}} {{qualifier|UK}}<!--Note: "sincerely" is not a synonym as it is used differently-->

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|unfaithfully}}

